{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>The two sons of Jacob.</b> They were his sons, and even so, Shimon and Levi conducted themselves like other men who are not his sons, for they took no counsel from him (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Brothers of Dinah.</b> Because they risked themselves for her, they are called her brothers." "<b>Securely.</b> They were in pain, and alternatively: they were confident in the strength of the old man (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {2 "The reading מ״א in the Hebrew is an abbreviation for ומ״א (= ומאן אחרינא, 'and alternatively')."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:05.608105408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}